{
  "_comment": "Dutch terms on the boards and the English used for them, once, so every catalogue says the same thing. Dutch government terms get their established English equivalent; where the Dutch abbreviation is the name foreigners meet (Woo, DigiD, BSN, KVK), it stays and the first use on a board spells it out. Product names (Dossiq, Pipelinq, Portaliq, Nextcloud, OpenProject, Zuiddrecht) are never translated. Names of people, streets, places, dates, times and amounts stay Dutch. English follows the Conduction voice: sentence case, no em-dashes, you and we, short sentences. British spelling (organisation, colour, licence).",
  "style": {
    "case": "Sentence case in every heading, button, tab and menu item. 'Mijn zaken' is 'My cases', never 'My Cases'.",
    "you": "Formal Dutch 'u' and informal 'je' both become 'you'. Keep the register of the board: resident-facing text is plain and warm, back-office text is terse.",
    "dates": "Numbers, times and amounts are left as drawn (13:59, € 24,50). Month and weekday names in English text are translated: 'Payroll run October 2026', 'Submitted 14 September 2026 by Sanne Mulder', 'Next run Fri 9 Oct 08:00', 'Weekly, on Monday', 'Mon to Fri'. A date cell standing alone that was left empty stays empty, as drawn. This replaces the earlier rule that month names stay Dutch.",
    "names": "Person names, street names, place names, mail addresses, reference numbers and file names stay as drawn. Organisation and party names stay Dutch (Groen Zuiddrecht, Fietsersbond, Bakkerij Van Dam). 'Gemeente X' as an organisation becomes 'Municipality of X', capitalised; as a token-set name in a thematiq picker it stays 'Gemeente X'.",
    "departments": "Department, team and committee names are translated (Publiekszaken: Public services, Burgerzaken: Civil affairs, Buitenruimte: Public space, Belastingen: Taxes, Vergunningen: Permits, Dienstverlening: Customer services, Bedrijfsvoering: Operations, Commissie Ruimte: Spatial planning committee). 'Team X' keeps the order as drawn: 'Team Parkeren' is 'Team Parking'.",
    "titles": "meneer and mevrouw become Mr and Ms; juf and meester before a name become Miss and Mr ('Miss Esra', 'Mr Daan'). Never Mrs.",
    "filter_labels": "'Filteren op <Kolom>' is 'Filter by <Column>', with the column name capitalised as drawn ('Filter by Status'). Never 'Filter on'.",
    "shared_strings": "A string in _common.json carries the meaning most boards give it. A board that means something else puts the string in its own catalogue as an override (see scripts/screens/README.md): Kassa is 'Till' in _common.json and 'Point of sale' on the module and menu boards.",
    "dashes": "No em-dash (—) and no double hyphen. Use a period, a comma or a colon.",
    "already_english": "A string that is already English is copied as it is, with sentence case and dashes fixed only when wrong."
  },
